#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD2238 expect=skipped domain=CE
#note "CESTDTC is not in the dataset (rule round 2026-10-12, var_exists sweep, owner 2026-10-07): the grouping key --STDTC moved from a Check-level var_exists guard into Requirements.Variables.All, so the rule is SKIPPED instead of passing silently (as PMDA-SD2238-skipped_no_stdtc_column). Red under the old rule (it ran: no violation). Without either gate the absent key drops out of [USUBJID, --STDTC] and the subject's two different CESTTPT values would fire."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset CE class=EVENTS label="Clinical Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col CESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col CETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Clinical Event"
col CESTTPT type=Char label="Start Reference Time Point"
---
S1 | CE | 001 | 1 | RASH  | SCREENING
S1 | CE | 001 | 2 | FEVER | RANDOMIZATION
